Solid State Physics — Steven H. Simon, 2012 draft (@mat-simon-solid: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_3R4Q71S31MD0EH6YVDQQ2ESKH5
Steven H. Simon, Oxford. [Author's course](https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/SteveSimon/condmat2015/condmat.html), [269-page draft dated 9 January 2012](https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/SteveSimon/condmat2012/LectureNotes2012.pdf), [draft corrections](https://www-thphys.physics.ox.ac.uk/people/SteveSimon/condmat2012/typos.html).

Read chapters 1–22, including exercises, then work the five course homeworks and revision problems. Chapter 23, Magnetic Devices, is explicitly unfinished in this draft; it cannot supply the application reading its title suggests. The author distinguishes the free draft from the corrected commercial book. Public lecture videos and examinations are linked by the course page; some university video access is restricted.

Cover, contents and selected vibrational, semiconductor and magnetic-interaction passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. The draft's strengths and omissions differ from Tong and MIT. Compare their assumptions rather than treating one curriculum as a complete field. Copyright remains with the author; no general open adaptation licence was established. Keep all source material external.

